</node>
<node id="Chu State">
  <data key="d0">Chu State</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Chu State is an ancient kingdom targeted by the Wu State, characterized by a network of rivers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-34a910155a4ca89cef37c9d03aa719e0</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513333</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="British Army">
  <data key="d0">British Army</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The British Army conducted environmental adaptability training to prepare for combat in harsh climates.&lt;SEP&gt;Historical military force noted for a deployment experience regarding climate adaptation in 1769.&lt;SEP&gt;Military force stationed in the West Indies that suffered high casualties due to disease and climate.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-34a910155a4ca89cef37c9d03aa719e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4069171df455529318ba9f6a609d862c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f503c5e9407265dde67c9f70d969bf19</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513333</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Norway">
  <data key="d0">Norway</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Norway is the location where the British Army undertook three months of geographical environmental adaptability training annually.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-34a910155a4ca89cef37c9d03aa719e0</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513333</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Malvinas Islands">
  <data key="d0">Malvinas Islands</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Malvinas Islands are the location of the battle where the British Army utilized preparedness for cold climates to achieve victory.&lt;SEP&gt;The Malvinas Islands are the location where a sovereignty dispute occurred between the United Kingdom and Argentina, triggering the Falklands War.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-34a910155a4ca89cef37c9d03aa719e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4d7d1f88fe246b51fd0303547d9be8d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513333</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Geographical Environment">
  <data key="d0">Geographical Environment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Geographical Environment determines the structure and size of armed forces and influences military strategy and battlefield preparation.&lt;SEP&gt;Geographical Environment is a critical factor determining combat forms, tactics, and battlefield preparation requirements across different scenarios.&lt;SEP&gt;Geographical Environment refers to the conditions under which wars are conducted and which influence and constrain military actions.&lt;SEP&gt;Geographical Environment refers to natural conditions such as terrain and climate that constrain military operations and training.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-34a910155a4ca89cef37c9d03aa719e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-273c61bc25c3835cb71ff0cd7a221bf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c596f93a800f01604d14372afd18ffb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bd22db232a2593a19ce46cb27abefe9</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513333</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Military Action">
  <data key="d0">Military Action</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Combat operations guided by geographical strategies and affected by environmental conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Military Action encompasses combat activities and strategic operations influenced by geographical factors.&lt;SEP&gt;Military Action encompasses operations affected by water systems, including obstacles in eastern China and resource shortages in western China.&lt;SEP&gt;Operational activities influenced by terrain factors such as movement, observation, shooting, and concealment.&lt;SEP&gt;Military action refers to strategic operations influenced by geographical features like river orientations.&lt;SEP&gt;Military Action is significantly influenced by climate factors such as temperature, precipitation, and wind patterns in China.&lt;SEP&gt;Military Action refers to operations impacted by climatic factors such as temperature, rainfall, and typhoons in different seasons.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-34a910155a4ca89cef37c9d03aa719e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0062bd3dbcdf5b7c925a5e3266bd885c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e567fa8fe0d09b8716b7c59ce0c8aaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b32dded5fc0150b9f8a563e98f31293&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2a34c49c188ba9a655c3c10d21458c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb7c5877c55d5fba2943b2f7e8e86409&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a79980cadb14f8eecf17a7424058f80a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513333</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Land Terrain">
  <data key="d0">Land Terrain</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Land Terrain is a specific category of geographical conditions affecting movement, deployment, and weapon effectiveness.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-34a910155a4ca89cef37c9d03aa719e0</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513333</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Plain">
  <data key="d0">Plain</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Plain is a flat terrain type that facilitates mechanized movement but offers little concealment and high vulnerability to weapons.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-34a910155a4ca89cef37c9d03aa719e0</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513333</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hill">
  <data key="d0">Hill</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Hill is a terrain type offering favorable conditions for both offense and defense, providing protection against certain weapons.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-34a910155a4ca89cef37c9d03aa719e0</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513333</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mountain">
  <data key="d0">Mountain</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Mountain is a rugged terrain suitable for defense and guerrilla warfare but restricts heavy machinery mobility.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-34a910155a4ca89cef37c9d03aa719e0</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513333</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Plateau">
  <data key="d0">Plateau</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Plateau is a high-altitude terrain that affects personnel health and logistics due to thin air and variable temperatures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-34a910155a4ca89cef37c9d03aa719e0</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513333</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Grassland">
  <data key="d0">Grassland</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Grassland is an open terrain beneficial for tank movement but lacks sufficient water and resources for troops.&lt;SEP&gt;Grassland terrain is characterized by a flat and open surface with slight undulations, facilitating tank movement and troop mobility despite challenges in observation and supply.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-34a910155a4ca89cef37c9d03aa719e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c80ee723bcf749b452d4339be150476c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513333</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nuclear Weapon">
  <data key="d0">Nuclear Weapon</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Nuclear Weapon is a strategic armament equipped on naval vessels like aircraft carriers since the mid-20th century.&lt;SEP&gt;Nuclear Weapon is a destructive armament whose hazard range is significantly larger in plain terrains compared to others.&lt;SEP&gt;Nuclear Weapon represents a threat in various terrains, causing fires via light radiation in grasslands and being a primary concern for residential area protection.&lt;SEP&gt;A weapon whose attack effects are influenced by terrain regarding shock waves and diffusion.&lt;SEP&gt;Nuclear Weapon is a category of weaponry included in the research scope of military meteorology impacts.&lt;SEP&gt;A weapon with five main effects including shockwaves and radiation, whose efficiency is heavily influenced by atmospheric conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-34a910155a4ca89cef37c9d03aa719e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04fe3e063b1934b10a4b54c4167a8091&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28485bea858dd98198f1090de689f18a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b32dded5fc0150b9f8a563e98f31293&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c80ee723bcf749b452d4339be150476c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c596f93a800f01604d14372afd18ffb</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513333</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Chemical Weapon">
  <data key="d0">Chemical Weapon</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Chemical Weapon involves agents that can be retained longer in valley and concave areas of hills and mountains.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemical Weapon is listed as a significant threat targeting residential areas due to their population concentration and infrastructure.&lt;SEP&gt;A weapon whose attack effects are influenced by terrain regarding agent diffusion and retention.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemical Weapon is a category of weaponry included in the research scope of military meteorology impacts.&lt;SEP&gt;Weapons utilizing toxic substances whose effectiveness varies greatly with temperature, precipitation, and wind direction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-34a910155a4ca89cef37c9d03aa719e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04fe3e063b1934b10a4b54c4167a8091&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28485bea858dd98198f1090de689f18a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b32dded5fc0150b9f8a563e98f31293&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c80ee723bcf749b452d4339be150476c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513333</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tank">
  <data key="d0">Tank</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Tank is a armored vehicle whose movement is facilitated by plains but restricted by water fields, mountains, and grasslands.&lt;SEP&gt;A Tank is a military vehicle whose mobility is favored by grassland and gobi terrain, though its tracks are susceptible to wear on gravel surfaces.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-34a910155a4ca89cef37c9d03aa719e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c80ee723bcf749b452d4339be150476c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513333</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Water Warfare Training">
  <data key="d0">Water Warfare Training</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Water Warfare Training is a specialized military drill designed by Sun Wu to counter the river-heavy geography of the Chu State.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-34a910155a4ca89cef37c9d03aa719e0</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513333</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adaptability Training">
  <data key="d0">Adaptability Training</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Adaptability Training is a regimen performed by the British Army in Norway to withstand extreme climatic threats during operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-34a910155a4ca89cef37c9d03aa719e0</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513333</data>
