<node id="Subtropical Forestland">
  <data key="d0">Subtropical Forestland</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Subtropical Forestland is a specific terrain type characterized by dense vegetation, fog, and high altitude, affecting health and communication.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-34a910155a4ca89cef37c9d03aa719e0</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513334</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Yangtze River">
  <data key="d0">Yangtze River</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">A major river where the upper reaches flow through the location of the Sichuan Basin.&lt;SEP&gt;The Yangtze River is the longest river in China, originating from the Tibetan Plateau and flowing into the East Sea.&lt;SEP&gt;The longest river in China, flowing 6300km through multiple provinces into the East China Sea, characterized by abundant water resources and high strategic value.&lt;SEP&gt;The Yangtze River is a major waterway located in the mid-lower reaches of the East Lake Region.&lt;SEP&gt;A major river system in China where the middle and lower reaches form a relatively stable precipitation belt during winter.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0b92052b83239097e641b25dcb4c198&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5526035222e5349787e63203c8c751d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2a34c49c188ba9a655c3c10d21458c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2067a05006e92d59f8bbb55189a87ea8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b3394b9b4e98f146bc3091517249c5b</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513334</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Yellow River">
  <data key="d0">Yellow River</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The Yellow River is a major northern river known for extremely high sediment content and transport volumes.&lt;SEP&gt;The second largest river in China, originating from Bayankala Mountain, flowing into Bohai Sea, historically significant for culture and prone to flooding.&lt;SEP&gt;The Yellow River is one of the significant river systems associated with the lake distribution in the East Lake Region.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0b92052b83239097e641b25dcb4c198&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2a34c49c188ba9a655c3c10d21458c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2067a05006e92d59f8bbb55189a87ea8</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513334</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Huai River">
  <data key="d0">Huai River</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">A river originating from Tongbai Mountain, flowing through Anhui and Jiangsu, splitting into the Yangtze and Yellow Sea, noted for concentrated rainfall and flood risks.&lt;SEP&gt;The Huai River is a watercourse whose downstream areas are part of the East Lake Region.&lt;SEP&gt;Huai River serves as a geographic boundary marking the 0°C isotherm during winter in China.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0b92052b83239097e641b25dcb4c198&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2067a05006e92d59f8bbb55189a87ea8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b3394b9b4e98f146bc3091517249c5b</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513334</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pearl River">
  <data key="d0">Pearl River</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">A major southern river system comprising Xijiang, Beijiang, and Dongjiang, flowing into the South China Sea, serving as a vital economic and transportation zone.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0b92052b83239097e641b25dcb4c198</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513334</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Heilongjiang River">
  <data key="d0">Heilongjiang River</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The Heilongjiang River forms part of the northern boundary between China and Russia.&lt;SEP&gt;A border river formed by the merger of Shilakhe and Erguna Rivers, flowing into the Sea of Okhotsk, acting as a northern barrier for China.&lt;SEP&gt;Heilongjiang River is a major river flowing eastwards into the Sea of Okhotsk, with a total length of 4370km and significant military significance as a barrier.&lt;SEP&gt;The Heilongjiang River forms a boundary between Northeast China and the Russian Far East.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0b92052b83239097e641b25dcb4c198&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2067a05006e92d59f8bbb55189a87ea8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8838d954c1b9dee27b68282526f5d2fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53a1e273402d0c5079e17bc3f132e9d2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513334</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="East China Sea">
  <data key="d0">East China Sea</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The East China Sea is one of the five major sea areas constituting China's maritime territory.&lt;SEP&gt;Located centrally in China's coastal area, the East China Sea facilitates north-south naval maneuverability and protects the Shanghai-Nanjing-Hangzhou region.&lt;SEP&gt;The body of water into which the Yangtze River flows.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0b92052b83239097e641b25dcb4c198&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98aa0a6c316255cf19e5c64b2770f024&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8838d954c1b9dee27b68282526f5d2fe</data>
