<node id="Bohai Sea">
  <data key="d0">Bohai Sea</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The Bohai Sea is an internal sea included within China's maritime territory.&lt;SEP&gt;The Bohai Sea is an enclosed inland sea of China, surrounded by the Liaodong and Shandong Peninsulas, significant for protecting the Beijing-Tianjin region.&lt;SEP&gt;A sea on the western side of the Liaodong Peninsula, an invasion route blocked by the Liaodong Hills.&lt;SEP&gt;The body of water into which the Yellow River flows.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0b92052b83239097e641b25dcb4c198&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98aa0a6c316255cf19e5c64b2770f024&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5526035222e5349787e63203c8c751d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8838d954c1b9dee27b68282526f5d2fe</data>
