  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="South China Sea">
  <data key="d0">South China Sea</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The South China Sea is one of the five major sea areas constituting China's maritime territory.&lt;SEP&gt;The South China Sea is the largest and southernmost extension of China's sea areas, serving as a strategic passage between the Pacific and Indian Oceans.&lt;SEP&gt;The South China Sea is the body of water surrounding the Nansha and Xisha Islands where sovereignty disputes occurred.&lt;SEP&gt;The body of water into which the Pearl River flows.&lt;SEP&gt;The South China Sea is a strategic waterway connecting the Pacific and Indian Oceans crucial for international shipping.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0b92052b83239097e641b25dcb4c198&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98aa0a6c316255cf19e5c64b2770f024&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dc9a717a7af0db2944d497cc6ed8276&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d53b857a7a2228ebfb7b675b22c9e4c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8838d954c1b9dee27b68282526f5d2fe</data>
