<node id="Greater Khingan Range">
  <data key="d0">Greater Khingan Range</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">A mountain range marking the boundary of the Second and Third Steps of the terrain.&lt;SEP&gt;The Greater Khingan Range is part of the dividing line between external and internal flow basins running from the Sino-Russian border.&lt;SEP&gt;A mountain range part of a sequence separating terrains, connected to Taihang, Wushan, and Xuefeng.&lt;SEP&gt;The westernmost row of the Northeast-Southwest oriented mountain ranges in eastern China.&lt;SEP&gt;The mountain range where the southern source of the Heilongjiang River originates.&lt;SEP&gt;The Greater Khingan Range is a mountainous region included in the humid climate zone and northeast area.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0b92052b83239097e641b25dcb4c198&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0062bd3dbcdf5b7c925a5e3266bd885c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5526035222e5349787e63203c8c751d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b32dded5fc0150b9f8a563e98f31293&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6540ee1693bb1952ff5f0c0a29a6cfda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb7c5877c55d5fba2943b2f7e8e86409</data>
