<node id="Wind">
  <data key="d0">Wind</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Wind is an atmospheric phenomenon used by Sun Quan and Liu Bei as a tactical advantage in the Battle of Chibi.&lt;SEP&gt;Wind is a natural meteorological element that affects ship navigation speed, aircraft flight dynamics, and missile trajectory.&lt;SEP&gt;Wind influences flight safety significantly, affecting takeoffs, landings, formation flying, and paratrooper deployment precision.&lt;SEP&gt;Wind is a movement of air that alters projectile speed and direction, causing deviations in landing points.&lt;SEP&gt;Wind is a natural phenomenon that influences artillery trajectory and sound propagation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ce0f8847579bcd84ebc6d7ccd5e3df71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f2d9cecd6bfddf0136042457124e4ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d33148b0d7436f29502a2e094038716&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc2492438202366534ec0b3b980991e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04fe3e063b1934b10a4b54c4167a8091</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513336</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Precipitation">
  <data key="d0">Precipitation</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Precipitation levels vary from over 2000mm in the southeast to under 250mm in the northwest, impacting water availability.&lt;SEP&gt;Precipitation refers to rainfall distribution which varies significantly between regions and seasons.&lt;SEP&gt;Precipitation includes rain and snow which reduce visibility and can affect aircraft control and braking distance on runways.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ce0f8847579bcd84ebc6d7ccd5e3df71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb7c5877c55d5fba2943b2f7e8e86409&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b3394b9b4e98f146bc3091517249c5b</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
