  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Visibility">
  <data key="d0">Visibility</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A measure of atmospheric transparency defining how far objects can be seen, categorized into several types.&lt;SEP&gt;Visibility is the distance at which objects can be seen clearly, reduced by clouds, rain, fog, and other atmospheric conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;A measure of clear sight distance in clouds that decreases with flight speed and cloud type, impacting pilot navigation and formation flying.&lt;SEP&gt;Visibility is the measure of atmospheric transparency which is reduced by various weather phenomena and affects weapon targeting.&lt;SEP&gt;Visibility is a measure of atmospheric clarity that determines the severity of radar range reduction during conditions like fog.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ce0f8847579bcd84ebc6d7ccd5e3df71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f2d9cecd6bfddf0136042457124e4ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d33148b0d7436f29502a2e094038716&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4069171df455529318ba9f6a609d862c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbf7b6b975f6c62ad2f6664872c40e85</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513336</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pilot">
  <data key="d0">Pilot</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Pilots operate aircraft and face challenges such as fatigue, instrument misreading, and spatial illusions caused by weather conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ce0f8847579bcd84ebc6d7ccd5e3df71</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513336</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Paratrooper">
  <data key="d0">Paratrooper</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Paratroopers are influenced by wind and vertical currents during descent, which can affect landing concentration and safety.&lt;SEP&gt;Paratroopers are military personnel whose landing safety is influenced by cloud height and visibility during jumps.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ce0f8847579bcd84ebc6d7ccd5e3df71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f2da0b5a925efce063af9f298932751</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513336</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cumulonimbus">
  <data key="d0">Cumulonimbus</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Cumulonimbus clouds are storm clouds that were monitored by meteorological personnel to determine safe flying windows during the 1969 incident.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ce0f8847579bcd84ebc6d7ccd5e3df71</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513336</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stratus Layer Cloud">
  <data key="d0">Stratus Layer Cloud</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Stratus Layer Clouds are layered clouds that were forecasted to arrive after 4 AM, allowing for a sortie window before their arrival.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ce0f8847579bcd84ebc6d7ccd5e3df71</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513336</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Japan">
  <data key="d0">Japan</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Japan is a smaller country with limited resources that cannot withstand prolonged warfare.&lt;SEP&gt;Japan is a country separated from China by the sea and possesses strong economic and military capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Japan is a country in the West Pacific used by the United States as part of the island chain strategy surrounding China.&lt;SEP&gt;Japan is a nation utilized by the United States in the Island Chain strategy and maintains security alliances with the US.&lt;SEP&gt;Japan is a country whose international shipping and freight heavily depend on routes through the South China Sea.&lt;SEP&gt;Nation declared war upon by the Soviet Union in August 1945 amidst the Manchurian rainy season.&lt;SEP&gt;Japan is the country where Tokyo is located and served as the target area for the 1944 B-29 bombing mission.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ce0f8847579bcd84ebc6d7ccd5e3df71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dc9a717a7af0db2944d497cc6ed8276&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-273c61bc25c3835cb71ff0cd7a221bf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8838d954c1b9dee27b68282526f5d2fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f503c5e9407265dde67c9f70d969bf19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a79980cadb14f8eecf17a7424058f80a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53a1e273402d0c5079e17bc3f132e9d2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513336</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Typhoon">
  <data key="d0">Typhoon</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Typhoon is a powerful tropical cyclone originating in specific regions that generates massive waves threatening navigation and aviation.&lt;SEP&gt;Typhoons are severe weather phenomena affecting southeastern China coastal areas, causing hazards to life, property, and defense facilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Typhoon is a severe weather event that threatens maritime navigation safety and hinders naval combat operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Typhoon is a tropical cyclone cited as a major hazard threatening ships and ports in naval warfare.&lt;SEP&gt;Typhoon is a severe wind condition mentioned as capable of destroying aircraft not protected by anti-typhoon measures.&lt;SEP&gt;A weather phenomenon that could be artificially guided to attack enemy ports and facilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ce0f8847579bcd84ebc6d7ccd5e3df71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04fe3e063b1934b10a4b54c4167a8091&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-172c6a0caad4a353ae3ab389f92c9a74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9f0cdb472c694c1c46ee77bdf461b98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f2da0b5a925efce063af9f298932751&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a79980cadb14f8eecf17a7424058f80a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513336</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mountains">
  <data key="d0">Mountains</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Mountainous areas produce complex wind currents like updrafts and downdrafts due to uneven heating.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ce0f8847579bcd84ebc6d7ccd5e3df71</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513337</data>
