<node id="Runway">
  <data key="d0">Runway</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The Runway is the surface where aircraft land and take off, affected by friction and weather conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Runways are surfaces where rain reduces friction and increases landing distance for aircraft.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ce0f8847579bcd84ebc6d7ccd5e3df71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f2d9cecd6bfddf0136042457124e4ff</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513337</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Turbine Compressor">
  <data key="d0">Turbine Compressor</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Turbine Compressor is part of jet engines that can experience thrust changes if rain droplets enter.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ce0f8847579bcd84ebc6d7ccd5e3df71</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513337</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Command Post">
  <data key="d0">Command Post</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The location where Eisenhower and high-ranking generals gathered to discuss weather and make decisions regarding the invasion date.&lt;SEP&gt;The Command Post coordinates military operations and receives reports from meteorological stations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ce0f8847579bcd84ebc6d7ccd5e3df71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbf7b6b975f6c62ad2f6664872c40e85</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513337</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fog">
  <data key="d0">Fog</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Fog is an atmospheric phenomenon used strategically by Zhuge Liang to hide activities and reduce visibility.&lt;SEP&gt;Weather condition reducing visibility that aided the Allied forces during the Dunkirk evacuation.&lt;SEP&gt;Fog is a weather condition that significantly aided the withdrawal of troops from Dunkirk.&lt;SEP&gt;Fog is a weather condition that lowers visibility and can mask parachutists and warplanes.&lt;SEP&gt;Fog is a weather phenomenon that significantly reduces visibility similar to clouds and rain.&lt;SEP&gt;Fog is a weather condition composed of water droplets that significantly shortens radar detection ranges.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ce0f8847579bcd84ebc6d7ccd5e3df71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f2d9cecd6bfddf0136042457124e4ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d33148b0d7436f29502a2e094038716&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc2492438202366534ec0b3b980991e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f503c5e9407265dde67c9f70d969bf19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f2da0b5a925efce063af9f298932751</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513337</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sandstorm">
  <data key="d0">Sandstorm</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Sandstorms cause electromagnetic wave attenuation and interfere with radio communication and equipment.&lt;SEP&gt;Sandstorm is a weather event that lowers visibility and protects ground troops from optical targeting.&lt;SEP&gt;Sandstorm is an atmospheric condition that affects flight visibility along with dust and haze.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ce0f8847579bcd84ebc6d7ccd5e3df71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f2d9cecd6bfddf0136042457124e4ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc2492438202366534ec0b3b980991e4</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
