  <data key="d5">1779513337</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ionosphere">
  <data key="d0">Ionosphere</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The Ionosphere is a layer of the atmosphere that affects radio wave propagation and can interrupt communications.&lt;SEP&gt;The Ionosphere is a layer of the atmosphere subject to disturbances caused by solar activity, affecting communication and navigation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-543b6633702af343c0b0d5a3a6321a00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d33148b0d7436f29502a2e094038716</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513337</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Solar Flare">
  <data key="d0">Solar Flare</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Solar flares emit electromagnetic radiation and high-energy protons that interfere with communications and damage satellites.&lt;SEP&gt;A solar flare is a sudden change on the Sun that releases high-energy protons and causes ionospheric disturbances.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-543b6633702af343c0b0d5a3a6321a00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12c0dfe1adf2b5c68db487a859f79f7a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513337</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Magnetic Storm">
  <data key="d0">Magnetic Storm</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">A magnetic storm is a severe space weather event driven by solar activity that can damage satellites and disrupt navigation.&lt;SEP&gt;Magnetic storm is a temporary disturbance of the Earth's magnetosphere caused by solar activity, posing risks to space operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-543b6633702af343c0b0d5a3a6321a00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12c0dfe1adf2b5c68db487a859f79f7a</data>
