  <data key="d0">Eurasian Continent</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Eurasian Continent is the large landmass where China is situated to the east, forming a primary geographic coordinate for regional military strategy.&lt;SEP&gt;The Eurasian Continent is the major landmass where China is geographically situated, influencing its continental connection.&lt;SEP&gt;The Eurasian Continent is the landmass where China is located, forming the eastern slope facing the Pacific Ocean.&lt;SEP&gt;Continent on which China is situated.&lt;SEP&gt;The Eurasian Continent extends westward from China and influences climate patterns through its interaction with the Pacific Ocean.&lt;SEP&gt;The Eurasian Continent is the largest landmass comprising Asia and Europe.</data>
