</node>
<node id="Liaodong Peninsula">
  <data key="d0">Liaodong Peninsula</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The Liaodong Peninsula is one of the two peninsulas enclosing the Bohai Sea, contributing to its closed nature.&lt;SEP&gt;A peninsula bordered by the Bohai Sea and Yellow Sea, strategically guarded by the Liaodong Hills.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-98aa0a6c316255cf19e5c64b2770f024&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5526035222e5349787e63203c8c751d2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513341</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Shandong Peninsula">
  <data key="d0">Shandong Peninsula</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The Shandong Peninsula encloses the Bohai Sea along with the Liaodong Peninsula, offering defensive advantages for the region.&lt;SEP&gt;A peninsula west of which lies the Yellow River and Grand Canal, protected by the Shandong Hills.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-98aa0a6c316255cf19e5c64b2770f024&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5526035222e5349787e63203c8c751d2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513341</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Korean Strait">
  <data key="d0">Korean Strait</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The Korean Strait is one of the critical waterways forming the island chain surrounding China's sea areas, connecting to the Japan Sea.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-98aa0a6c316255cf19e5c64b2770f024</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513341</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
