</node>
<node id="Bashi Strait">
  <data key="d0">Bashi Strait</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The Bashi Strait is a vital passageway controlling access to and from China's southern sea regions towards the Pacific.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-98aa0a6c316255cf19e5c64b2770f024</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513341</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Malacca Strait">
  <data key="d0">Malacca Strait</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The Malacca Strait is a key maritime chokepoint connecting China's sea areas to the Indian Ocean, controlled by maritime powers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-98aa0a6c316255cf19e5c64b2770f024</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513341</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Indian Ocean">
  <data key="d0">Indian Ocean</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Indian Ocean is a sea region known for a catastrophic earthquake and tsunami event in 2004 that resulted in widespread devastation across neighboring countries.&lt;SEP&gt;The Indian Ocean connects with the South China Sea and serves as a route for trade and strategic dynamics in the Asia-Pacific region.&lt;SEP&gt;The Indian Ocean receives flow from some of China's external flow rivers located in southern regions.&lt;SEP&gt;The Indian Ocean receives flow from outer-flowing rivers in southern China.&lt;SEP&gt;The Indian Ocean is connected to the South China Sea via strategic shipping routes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-98aa0a6c316255cf19e5c64b2770f024&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dc9a717a7af0db2944d497cc6ed8276&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0062bd3dbcdf5b7c925a5e3266bd885c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2a34c49c188ba9a655c3c10d21458c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9f0cdb472c694c1c46ee77bdf461b98</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513341</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sino-Indian Border">
  <data key="d0">Sino-Indian Border</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The Sino-Indian Border is a disputed boundary line divided into Eastern, Central, and Western sections, historically following traditional administrative limits.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-98aa0a6c316255cf19e5c64b2770f024</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513341</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="McMahon Line">
  <data key="d0">McMahon Line</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The McMahon Line is a boundary demarcated secretly in 1914 by Henry McMahon, assigning Chinese territory to British India.&lt;SEP&gt;The McMahon Line is a boundary line drawn along the Himalayan watershed that separates traditional Chinese territory from British India.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-98aa0a6c316255cf19e5c64b2770f024&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d53b857a7a2228ebfb7b675b22c9e4c6</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513341</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Henry McMahon">
  <data key="d0">Henry McMahon</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Henry McMahon was the Foreign Minister of British India who formulated the controversial McMahon Line during negotiations in New Delhi.&lt;SEP&gt;Henry McMahon is the British Foreign Secretary of British India who formulated the McMahon Line.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-98aa0a6c316255cf19e5c64b2770f024&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d53b857a7a2228ebfb7b675b22c9e4c6</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513341</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="British India">
  <data key="d0">British India</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">British India was the colonial administration ruled by the UK that engaged in secret correspondence regarding the Sino-Indian border.&lt;SEP&gt;British India is the colonial administration that exchanged notes with local governments in New Delhi regarding the boundary.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-98aa0a6c316255cf19e5c64b2770f024&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d53b857a7a2228ebfb7b675b22c9e4c6</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513341</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="People's Republic Of China">
  <data key="d0">People's Republic Of China</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The People's Republic of China resolved many border issues with neighbors after its establishment, though some disputes like the Sino-Indian border remain.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-98aa0a6c316255cf19e5c64b2770f024</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513341</data>
