<node id="Himalayas">
  <data key="d0">Himalayas</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The Himalayas mountain range hosts the Eastern segment of the traditional Sino-Indian customary boundary line.&lt;SEP&gt;The Himalayas is the mountain range along the watershed where the McMahon Line was drawn.&lt;SEP&gt;A mountain range in the west of China, completing the north-to-south sequence with Altai and Qilian.&lt;SEP&gt;A major mountain range in the northwest-southeast row distributed in western China.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-98aa0a6c316255cf19e5c64b2770f024&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d53b857a7a2228ebfb7b675b22c9e4c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5526035222e5349787e63203c8c751d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b32dded5fc0150b9f8a563e98f31293</data>
