<node id="Military Meteorology">
  <data key="d0">Military Meteorology</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Military Meteorology is the study of atmospheric conditions relevant to military operations and weapon performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Military Meteorology is a discipline studying the impact of weather conditions on military actions and equipment, formed based on military and meteorological science.&lt;SEP&gt;The study and application of meteorological science specifically for military operations and weather support.&lt;SEP&gt;Military Meteorology is the study of meteorological conditions and their impact on military activities, weapons, and engineering.&lt;SEP&gt;Military Meteorology is the study of meteorological conditions impacting military activities, weapon effectiveness, and operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Military Meteorology is the study and application of weather data to support military operations and planning.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5dc9a717a7af0db2944d497cc6ed8276&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd4b77ddbad65d9e33f870d31b0a2ed1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc2492438202366534ec0b3b980991e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04fe3e063b1934b10a4b54c4167a8091&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-003994fca557bfd14758df9f40939adf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4069171df455529318ba9f6a609d862c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513343</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
