  <data key="d0">Parachutist</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Parachutists are military personnel who benefit from low visibility conditions that cover their presence.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4f2d9cecd6bfddf0136042457124e4ff</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513346</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Optical Aiming Weapon">
  <data key="d0">Optical Aiming Weapon</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Optical Aiming Weapons are systems whose effectiveness is reduced by low visibility conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4f2d9cecd6bfddf0136042457124e4ff</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513347</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Radar Guided Weapon">
  <data key="d0">Radar Guided Weapon</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Radar Guided Weapons are systems that are not affected by low visibility conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4f2d9cecd6bfddf0136042457124e4ff</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513347</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GPS Guided Weapon">
  <data key="d0">GPS Guided Weapon</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">GPS Guided Weapons are navigation systems that remain functional despite low visibility conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4f2d9cecd6bfddf0136042457124e4ff</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513347</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ground Artillery">
  <data key="d0">Ground Artillery</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Ground Artillery refers to cannons used on the ground whose shooting accuracy is influenced by meteorological conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4f2d9cecd6bfddf0136042457124e4ff</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513347</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Anti-Aircraft Gun">
  <data key="d0">Anti-Aircraft Gun</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Anti-Aircraft Gun is a high-altitude firing weapon sensitive to temperature, air density, and wind variations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4f2d9cecd6bfddf0136042457124e4ff</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513347</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="100 mm Anti-Aircraft Gun">
  <data key="d0">100 mm Anti-Aircraft Gun</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The 100 mm Anti-Aircraft Gun is a specific caliber weapon where temperature increases significantly alter firing range and height.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4f2d9cecd6bfddf0136042457124e4ff</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513347</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Projectile">
  <data key="d0">Projectile</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Projectile is the shell fired by artillery that travels through the air subject to drag, wind, and temperature effects.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4f2d9cecd6bfddf0136042457124e4ff</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513347</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Atmospheric Pressure">
  <data key="d0">Atmospheric Pressure</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Atmospheric Pressure is a meteorological element that determines air density and influences projectile resistance and landing point.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4f2d9cecd6bfddf0136042457124e4ff</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513347</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Air Density">
  <data key="d0">Air Density</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Air Density is an atmospheric property that influences the range of early nuclear radiation and light radiation impulses.&lt;SEP&gt;Air Density is the mass of air per unit volume, affected by pressure and temperature, determining aerodynamic drag on projectiles.&lt;SEP&gt;Air Density is a meteorological factor explicitly listed alongside temperature and pressure that affects artillery ballistics and wave propagation.&lt;SEP&gt;A physical property of the atmosphere influenced by temperature, affecting the propagation of Early Radiation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4f2d9cecd6bfddf0136042457124e4ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d33148b0d7436f29502a2e094038716&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28485bea858dd98198f1090de689f18a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-003994fca557bfd14758df9f40939adf</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513347</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Temperature">
  <data key="d0">Temperature</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Temperature is a key climate element measured in various zones, affecting crop maturity and military operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Temperature is a climatic factor that fluctuates across latitudes and seasons affecting operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Temperature is a meteorological element influencing radio wave propagation distance and ship crew operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Temperature is a weather factor that affects air density, fire powder combustion rate, and fuse timing.&lt;SEP&gt;Temperature is a atmospheric factor that impacts acoustics, radar refraction, and material performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4f2d9cecd6bfddf0136042457124e4ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d33148b0d7436f29502a2e094038716&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04fe3e063b1934b10a4b54c4167a8091&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb7c5877c55d5fba2943b2f7e8e86409&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b3394b9b4e98f146bc3091517249c5b</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513347</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Virtual Temperature">
  <data key="d0">Virtual Temperature</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Virtual Temperature is a meteorological factor affecting the trajectory and landing point of artillery shells.&lt;SEP&gt;Virtual Temperature is a corrected temperature value used to account for humidity effects on air density calculations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4f2d9cecd6bfddf0136042457124e4ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04fe3e063b1934b10a4b54c4167a8091</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513347</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Drag">
  <data key="d0">Drag</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Drag is the air resistance force acting on a projectile, determined by shape, air density, and meteorological conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4f2d9cecd6bfddf0136042457124e4ff</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513347</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Trajectory">
  <data key="d0">Trajectory</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Trajectory is the path of the projectile which is determined by launch angle, initial velocity, and environmental forces.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4f2d9cecd6bfddf0136042457124e4ff</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513347</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="T-5 Fuse">
  <data key="d0">T-5 Fuse</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The T-5 Fuse is a specific type of firearm fuze where action time shortens as temperature increases.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4f2d9cecd6bfddf0136042457124e4ff</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513347</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fuse">
  <data key="d0">Fuse</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Fuse is a mechanism in ordnance affected by temperature and pressure, controlling detonation timing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4f2d9cecd6bfddf0136042457124e4ff</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513348</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Humidity">
  <data key="d0">Humidity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Humidity is a meteorological factor inversely related to air density, affecting calculations via virtual temperature.&lt;SEP&gt;Humidity is an atmospheric condition that influences electromagnetic wave transmission and equipment durability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4f2d9cecd6bfddf0136042457124e4ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d33148b0d7436f29502a2e094038716</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513348</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Smoke Screen">
  <data key="d0">Smoke Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">A tactical measure deployed in naval combat that relies heavily on atmospheric factors such as wind, temperature, and humidity.&lt;SEP&gt;Smoke Screen is a weather condition that lowers visibility and masks units like parachutists.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4f2d9cecd6bfddf0136042457124e4ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbf7b6b975f6c62ad2f6664872c40e85</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513348</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Haze">
  <data key="d0">Haze</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Haze is a weather phenomenon that reduces visibility alongside clouds, rain, and fog.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4f2d9cecd6bfddf0136042457124e4ff</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513348</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Floating Dust">
  <data key="d0">Floating Dust</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Floating Dust is an atmospheric condition that decreases visibility and influences battlefield observation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4f2d9cecd6bfddf0136042457124e4ff</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513348</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Explosion Point">
  <data key="d0">Explosion Point</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Explosion Point is the detonation location of a projectile, affected by temperature, wind, and fuse settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4f2d9cecd6bfddf0136042457124e4ff</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513348</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Initial Velocity">
  <data key="d0">Initial Velocity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Initial Velocity is the speed of a projectile at launch, influenced by temperature and determining trajectory height.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4f2d9cecd6bfddf0136042457124e4ff</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513348</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Launch Angle">
  <data key="d0">Launch Angle</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Launch Angle determines the trajectory path along with initial velocity and flight resistance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4f2d9cecd6bfddf0136042457124e4ff</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513348</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Warplane">
  <data key="d0">Warplane</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Warplane is a combat aircraft protected by low visibility conditions from optical targeting weapons.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4f2d9cecd6bfddf0136042457124e4ff</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513348</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Water System">
  <data key="d0">Water System</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Water System refers to the complex network of rivers, lakes, marshes, and glaciers within China, providing both obstacles and resources for military operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0062bd3dbcdf5b7c925a5e3266bd885c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513349</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="External Flow River">
  <data key="d0">External Flow River</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">External Flow Rivers are rivers that drain into oceans, covering 63.8% of China's total area and flowing towards the Pacific, Indian, or Arctic Oceans.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0062bd3dbcdf5b7c925a5e3266bd885c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513349</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Internal Flow River">
  <data key="d0">Internal Flow River</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Internal Flow Rivers disappear inland and cover 36.2% of China's total area, with the exception of the Ertix River flowing through Kazakhstan.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0062bd3dbcdf5b7c925a5e3266bd885c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513349</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Arctic Ocean">
  <data key="d0">Arctic Ocean</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The Arctic Ocean is reached by the Ertix River, which originates in Xinjiang and passes through Kazakhstan.&lt;SEP&gt;The Arctic Ocean receives a small portion of outer-flowing rivers in northern China.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0062bd3dbcdf5b7c925a5e3266bd885c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2a34c49c188ba9a655c3c10d21458c3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513349</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Defense Strategy">
  <data key="d0">Defense Strategy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Defense Strategy utilizes large rivers and medium-sized rivers as strategic barriers to delay enemy advances.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0062bd3dbcdf5b7c925a5e3266bd885c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513349</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Attack Strategy">
  <data key="d0">Attack Strategy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Attack Strategy faces challenges from large rivers which act as obstacles slowing down progress and segmenting combat formations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0062bd3dbcdf5b7c925a5e3266bd885c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513349</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Transportation Infrastructure">
  <data key="d0">Transportation Infrastructure</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Transportation Infrastructure includes railways and highway bridges necessary for crossing vast water systems, facilitating troop mobility and supply transport.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0062bd3dbcdf5b7c925a5e3266bd885c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513349</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nuclear And Chemical Weapons">
  <data key="d0">Nuclear And Chemical Weapons</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Nuclear And Chemical Weapons require large amounts of water for decontamination purposes during combat operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0062bd3dbcdf5b7c925a5e3266bd885c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
