</node>
<node id="Lake Count Data">
  <data key="d0">Lake Count Data</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Lake Count Data records over 2,800 lakes in China with areas exceeding 1 square kilometer.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0062bd3dbcdf5b7c925a5e3266bd885c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513349</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Total Lake Area Data">
  <data key="d0">Total Lake Area Data</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Total Lake Area Data shows that the total surface area of lakes in China reaches 80,000 square kilometers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0062bd3dbcdf5b7c925a5e3266bd885c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513349</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Qinling Mountains">
  <data key="d0">Qinling Mountains</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">A mountain range bordering the north side of the Sichuan Basin.&lt;SEP&gt;The Qinling Mountains mark a boundary line where river network density and precipitation levels change significantly between north and south.&lt;SEP&gt;A mountain range that, with Dabie, separates western terrain formations like the Loess Plateau.&lt;SEP&gt;The Qinling Mountains are a key geographical boundary separating humid/subtropical regions from other climate zones in China.&lt;SEP&gt;Qinling Mountains form part of the geographic boundary dividing northern freezing and southern non-freezing zones.&lt;SEP&gt;The Qinling Mountains form a climatic boundary in China, with areas south seeing higher temperatures in autumn.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0062bd3dbcdf5b7c925a5e3266bd885c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5526035222e5349787e63203c8c751d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b32dded5fc0150b9f8a563e98f31293&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb7c5877c55d5fba2943b2f7e8e86409&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b3394b9b4e98f146bc3091517249c5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a79980cadb14f8eecf17a7424058f80a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513349</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="East China Region">
  <data key="d0">East China Region</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The East China Region is characterized by prominent water system obstacles but abundant water sources.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0062bd3dbcdf5b7c925a5e3266bd885c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513350</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="West China Region">
  <data key="d0">West China Region</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The West China Region generally lacks water system obstacles but suffers from water scarcity affecting military operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0062bd3dbcdf5b7c925a5e3266bd885c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513350</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="National Defense">
  <data key="d0">National Defense</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">National Defense relies on the natural conditions of China's territory for strategic barriers and operational flexibility.&lt;SEP&gt;National Defense encompasses the security infrastructure of China, which benefits from the water system's economic and strategic advantages.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0062bd3dbcdf5b7c925a5e3266bd885c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8838d954c1b9dee27b68282526f5d2fe</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513350</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="River Network Density">
  <data key="d0">River Network Density</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">River Network Density measures the concentration of rivers in a region, varying significantly between eastern and western China.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0062bd3dbcdf5b7c925a5e3266bd885c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513350</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Yinshan Mountains">
  <data key="d0">Yinshan Mountains</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Mountain range contributing to the strategic defense of the Three-North Regions.&lt;SEP&gt;Part of the northern row of east-west oriented mountain ranges in China.&lt;SEP&gt;A mountain range that helps separate the western side forming Inner Mongolia Plateau and Loess Plateau.&lt;SEP&gt;The Yinshan Mountains are part of the geographical dividing line between external and internal flow basins in China.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0062bd3dbcdf5b7c925a5e3266bd885c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5526035222e5349787e63203c8c751d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b32dded5fc0150b9f8a563e98f31293&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6540ee1693bb1952ff5f0c0a29a6cfda</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513350</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ertix River">
  <data key="d0">Ertix River</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The Ertix River is a specific river located in Xinjiang that flows through Kazakhstan into the Arctic Ocean.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0062bd3dbcdf5b7c925a5e3266bd885c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513350</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Kazakhstan">
  <data key="d0">Kazakhstan</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Kazakhstan is the country through which the Ertix River passes before reaching the Arctic Ocean.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0062bd3dbcdf5b7c925a5e3266bd885c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513350</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Guerrilla Warfare">
  <data key="d0">Guerrilla Warfare</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Guerrilla Warfare is a combat form adopted by the Red Army when weak, involving tactics like retreating against attacks and striking when the enemy is tired.&lt;SEP&gt;Guerrilla Warfare is a military tactic implemented by the Red Army under Mao Zedong's strategy during the land revolution.&lt;SEP&gt;Guerrilla Warfare is a combat style particularly favored by the complex terrain of the Yunnan-Guizhou Plateau.&lt;SEP&gt;Guerrilla Warfare is a military tactic that finds convenience in plain water network regions with numerous lakes and marshes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0062bd3dbcdf5b7c925a5e3266bd885c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0902a5c933272b09fcdd85d68e45240&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-273c61bc25c3835cb71ff0cd7a221bf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bd22db232a2593a19ce46cb27abefe9</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513350</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ordos Plateau">
  <data key="d0">Ordos Plateau</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The Ordos Plateau is a region within China classified as having a small internal flow area.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0062bd3dbcdf5b7c925a5e3266bd885c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513350</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Yamdrok Lake">
  <data key="d0">Yamdrok Lake</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Yamdrok Lake is located south of the Yarlung Tsangpo River and represents a small internal flow area in Tibet.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0062bd3dbcdf5b7c925a5e3266bd885c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
