<node id="Meteorological Conditions">
  <data key="d0">Meteorological Conditions</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Specific atmospheric states that influence military training, planning, and combat operations.&lt;SEP&gt;General environmental factors including temperature and precipitation that significantly influence land warfare tactics.&lt;SEP&gt;Meteorological conditions refer to environmental factors such as temperature, wind, and pressure that affect military operations and equipment.&lt;SEP&gt;Meteorological Conditions refer to environmental factors like rain, fog, and cloud cover that affect weapon systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Environmental factors such as thunderstorms, strong winds, and humidity that significantly impact military operations and weapon effectiveness.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d33148b0d7436f29502a2e094038716&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4d7d1f88fe246b51fd0303547d9be8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28485bea858dd98198f1090de689f18a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4069171df455529318ba9f6a609d862c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f503c5e9407265dde67c9f70d969bf19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-003994fca557bfd14758df9f40939adf</data>
