<node id="Radar">
  <data key="d0">Radar</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Radar is equipment used by meteorological departments alongside satellite data to analyze weather for mission planning.&lt;SEP&gt;Equipment affected by meteorological conditions during military operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Radar is detection equipment generally installed on existing modern ships to monitor atmospheric conditions and targets.&lt;SEP&gt;Equipment installed on existing vessels whose performance is significantly influenced by low-level atmospheric weather conditions like temperature and humidity.&lt;SEP&gt;Radar is a detection system whose sensitivity and range are affected by atmospheric microstructures and weather conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Radar systems installed on naval vessels are electronic devices vulnerable to interference from weather conditions like rain and sea spray.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d33148b0d7436f29502a2e094038716&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28b68cb8b3fe687d054eb5d09604e0ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4d7d1f88fe246b51fd0303547d9be8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4069171df455529318ba9f6a609d862c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f2da0b5a925efce063af9f298932751&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbf7b6b975f6c62ad2f6664872c40e85</data>
