<node id="Guidance System">
  <data key="d0">Guidance System</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Guidance System controls Precision-Guided Weapons and emits or receives electromagnetic waves for targeting.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d33148b0d7436f29502a2e094038716</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513355</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Electromagnetic Waves">
  <data key="d0">Electromagnetic Waves</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Electromagnetic Waves are used for guidance and radar but suffer attenuation and scattering in the atmosphere.&lt;SEP&gt;Electromagnetic Waves are signals used for tracking and guidance that suffer attenuation when propagating through the atmosphere.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d33148b0d7436f29502a2e094038716&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4d7d1f88fe246b51fd0303547d9be8d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513355</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sound Waves">
  <data key="d0">Sound Waves</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Sound Waves transmit acoustic information for reconnaissance and are bent or weakened by temperature and wind gradients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d33148b0d7436f29502a2e094038716</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513355</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Acoustic Reconnaissance">
  <data key="d0">Acoustic Reconnaissance</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Acoustic Reconnaissance is a method of determining enemy positions using sound, heavily influenced by meteorological conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d33148b0d7436f29502a2e094038716</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513355</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Atmosphere">
  <data key="d0">Atmosphere</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The atmosphere is the physical environment that influences missile aerodynamics, navigation, and guidance systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The Atmosphere is the medium through which waves travel and provides resistance causing attenuation and refraction.&lt;SEP&gt;The Atmosphere is the layer of gases surrounding the Earth which attenuates and scatters electromagnetic waves during transmission.&lt;SEP&gt;The Atmospheric layer contains the ozone layer and serves as the medium where weather modification occurs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d33148b0d7436f29502a2e094038716&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4d7d1f88fe246b51fd0303547d9be8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-003994fca557bfd14758df9f40939adf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86b3997480c8d2d8abb49b09b2247575</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513356</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Optics Guidance">
  <data key="d0">Optics Guidance</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Optics Guidance is a method where weapons track targets using visible light, constrained by atmospheric visibility.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d33148b0d7436f29502a2e094038716</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513356</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Infrared Guidance">
  <data key="d0">Infrared Guidance</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Infrared Guidance is a method that tracks target heat radiation, subject to atmospheric thermal constraints.&lt;SEP&gt;Infrared Guidance is a targeting method that utilizes thermal radiation and focuses on specific wavelength bands to penetrate the atmosphere.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d33148b0d7436f29502a2e094038716&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4d7d1f88fe246b51fd0303547d9be8d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513356</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Laser Guidance">
  <data key="d0">Laser Guidance</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Laser Guidance is a method utilizing laser beams for targeting, which can be scattered by weather particles.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d33148b0d7436f29502a2e094038716</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513356</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Radar Guidance">
  <data key="d0">Radar Guidance</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Radar Guidance is a method using radar waves to steer weapons, affected by meteorological clutter.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d33148b0d7436f29502a2e094038716</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513356</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Static Electricity">
  <data key="d0">Static Electricity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Static Electricity is an electrical interference source mentioned alongside lightning that disrupts communication links and radio stations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d33148b0d7436f29502a2e094038716</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513356</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Water Particles">
  <data key="d0">Water Particles</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Water Particles are the physical microstructure of clouds, fog, and rain responsible for absorbing and scattering electromagnetic waves.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d33148b0d7436f29502a2e094038716</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513356</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Display">
  <data key="d0">Display</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Display is a radar component where echo images and false targets caused by meteorological interference are visualized.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d33148b0d7436f29502a2e094038716</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513356</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Thunderstorm">
  <data key="d0">Thunderstorm</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Thunderstorm is a severe weather phenomenon that poses risks to aircraft safety and operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Thunderstorm is a severe weather phenomenon containing lightning and turbulence that poses risks to flight safety and aircraft.&lt;SEP&gt;Thunderstorms are severe weather events capable of lowering radar component performance or causing physical damage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d33148b0d7436f29502a2e094038716&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04fe3e063b1934b10a4b54c4167a8091&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f2da0b5a925efce063af9f298932751</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513356</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ground">
  <data key="d0">Ground</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The Ground acts as a physical boundary influencing radar wave refraction and serves as a reference for ground-target detection.&lt;SEP&gt;The surface of the earth that receives sunlight, is targeted by lightning induction, or experiences environmental changes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d33148b0d7436f29502a2e094038716&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86b3997480c8d2d8abb49b09b2247575</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513356</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Weather Conditions">
  <data key="d0">Weather Conditions</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Weather conditions refer to atmospheric factors such as wind, rain, fog, and clouds that influence military operations, safety, and effectiveness.&lt;SEP&gt;Environmental factors including temperature, humidity, wind, and pressure that directly impact radar, smoke screens, and military operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Weather conditions encompass factors like temperature, pressure, humidity, wind, and rain that impact military operations and weapon efficacy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fc2492438202366534ec0b3b980991e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d401bd037e25faec28496db8f738e15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbf7b6b975f6c62ad2f6664872c40e85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-003994fca557bfd14758df9f40939adf</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513356</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
