</node>
<node id="Sun Quan">
  <data key="d0">Sun Quan</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Sun Quan was a ruler to whom an alliance was proposed as part of the strategic decision to unify the nation.&lt;SEP&gt;Sun Quan was a warlord who allied with Liu Bei to fight against Cao Cao using meteorological tactics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fc2492438202366534ec0b3b980991e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-273c61bc25c3835cb71ff0cd7a221bf0</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513357</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Liu Bei">
  <data key="d0">Liu Bei</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Liu Bei was a warlord who visited Zhuge Liang three times to seek strategies for unifying the nation.&lt;SEP&gt;Liu Bei was a warlord who allied with Sun Quan in the Battle of Chibi to defeat the enemy forces.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fc2492438202366534ec0b3b980991e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-273c61bc25c3835cb71ff0cd7a221bf0</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513357</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cao Cao">
  <data key="d0">Cao Cao</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Cao Cao was a rival warlord whose forces were to be confronted according to the strategic plan involving Jingzhou and Yizhou.&lt;SEP&gt;Cao Cao led the army that was defeated at the Battle of Chibi due to unfavorable weather conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fc2492438202366534ec0b3b980991e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-273c61bc25c3835cb71ff0cd7a221bf0</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
