<node id="Military Geography">
  <data key="d0">Military Geography</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Science studying the mutual relationship between military actions and geographical environments, comprising theoretical and applied parts.&lt;SEP&gt;Military Geography is the study of geographical environments relevant to military operations, including land, sea, air, and space domains.&lt;SEP&gt;Military Geography is a discipline whose research scope extends from ground and water surfaces to underground, underwater, and outer space.&lt;SEP&gt;Military Geography is a discipline examining the strategic value of natural conditions such as terrain, climate, territory, and maritime access for defense purposes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e567fa8fe0d09b8716b7c59ce0c8aaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-273c61bc25c3835cb71ff0cd7a221bf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c596f93a800f01604d14372afd18ffb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9f0cdb472c694c1c46ee77bdf461b98</data>
