<node id="United States">
  <data key="d0">United States</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The United States is a major global superpower characterized by extensive economic and military presence, particularly within the Asia-Pacific and Western Pacific regions. Following World War II, the nation established control over these areas, proposing strategic concepts such as the Island Chain and Unstable Arc to contain China. As part of its logistical network, the United States imports critical strategic materials, including rubber and petroleum, via the South China Sea.

Historically, the United States demonstrated significant technological and military leadership. The country was responsible for launching the first experimental weather satellite in 1960 and subsequently led the multinational coalition forces during Gulf War operations. These actions highlight its long-standing role in directing international military efforts and advancing space technology.

In contemporary developments, the United States continues to function as a developed nation actively adjusting its military space strategies. This ongoing adaptation involves forming new aerospace forces to maintain superiority and address evolving security requirements in the modern era.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5dc9a717a7af0db2944d497cc6ed8276&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd4b77ddbad65d9e33f870d31b0a2ed1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28b68cb8b3fe687d054eb5d09604e0ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4d7d1f88fe246b51fd0303547d9be8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8838d954c1b9dee27b68282526f5d2fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a79980cadb14f8eecf17a7424058f80a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12c0dfe1adf2b5c68db487a859f79f7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53a1e273402d0c5079e17bc3f132e9d2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
