<node id="Pacific Ocean">
  <data key="d0">Pacific Ocean</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The Pacific Ocean is a major ocean body situated to the east and southeast of China, forming a significant maritime boundary along the eastern slope of the Eurasian Continent. As the ocean located east of the continent facing China, it connects directly to adjacent bodies of water, including the Japan Sea and the South China Sea. This geographical positioning establishes the Pacific Ocean as the primary body of water bordering China to the east.

In terms of hydrology and climate, the Pacific Ocean serves as the primary destination for the majority of outer-flowing rivers in China, specifically accounting for 56% of the national territory's drainage. Its presence contributes significantly to the continental monsoon climate through sea-land differences, while exhibiting varied environmental conditions including calm equatorial zones and stormy latitudes. Additionally, the ocean remains connected to China's sea areas, playing a vital role in maritime transport and strategic movement.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca32d9edb8f2ea2552786cd5c0728420&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98aa0a6c316255cf19e5c64b2770f024&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dc9a717a7af0db2944d497cc6ed8276&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0062bd3dbcdf5b7c925a5e3266bd885c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2a34c49c188ba9a655c3c10d21458c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6540ee1693bb1952ff5f0c0a29a6cfda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8838d954c1b9dee27b68282526f5d2fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb7c5877c55d5fba2943b2f7e8e86409&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9f0cdb472c694c1c46ee77bdf461b98</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779513371</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
