<node id="Russia">
  <data key="d0">Russia</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Russia is a nation state located on the Eurasia Continent that shares a land border with China and holds significant military power in the region. Its geography encompasses the Heilongjiang River, which flows through its territory and empties into the Sea of Okhotsk. In terms of commerce, Russia operates shipping routes connecting Europe to the Pacific Ocean through the South China Sea. Geopolitically, the country is included within the Unstable Arc and competes with the United States for hegemony. Following the dissolution of the Warsaw Pact, Russia continues to maintain strong military power on the Eurasia Continent.

In the specific domain of defense, Russia established its own aerospace force in response to the US military space stance. It collaborates on international security, such as when it was one of the two nations participating in the Peace Mission 2005 joint military exercise alongside China. Historically, Russia is a nation state that engaged in a multi-nation war in the mid-19th century. During this period, specifically in the Crimean War, it fought against the United Kingdom, France, and others. Additionally, the location served as the site where Napoleon's army suffered non-combat casualties due to unsuitable climate conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5dc9a717a7af0db2944d497cc6ed8276&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc2492438202366534ec0b3b980991e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28b68cb8b3fe687d054eb5d09604e0ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-003994fca557bfd14758df9f40939adf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2067a05006e92d59f8bbb55189a87ea8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88cb8c96ba6affc4bd44f5647b2408ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8838d954c1b9dee27b68282526f5d2fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a79980cadb14f8eecf17a7424058f80a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12c0dfe1adf2b5c68db487a859f79f7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53a1e273402d0c5079e17bc3f132e9d2</data>
